{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106230","id":2510963927,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6VqkTX","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106230","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106230.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106230.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106230","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106230/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106230/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106230/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/a6f7631ad95642db54a646df30079b54aa70431d","number":106230,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add a deferred rendering mode to the Forward+ renderer","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is a proof of concept implementation for a deferred clustered renderer as an option in the Forward+ renderer of Godot.\r\nYou can enable deferred rendering in the project settings (Driver section, below depth prepass setting).\r\n\r\nIt changes the existing scene shader and skips the directional and positional lighting stages instead writing out data to a set of g-buffers (currently albedo, position, normal and ORM data).\r\nWe also write out ambient and GI data to our color buffer, there may be a case for moving this in a separate pass as well but it seems overkill at this point.\r\n\r\nThe lighting code has now moved to a post process. This is a compute shader that reads the data from the g-buffers and sets things up as if we're continuing the fragment shader of the scene shader. Then applies the same lighting code.\r\n\r\nThe transparent pass uses the normal forward approach, deferred is only applied for opaque rendering.\r\n\r\nThe current solution works with depth pre-pass however it may be more performant to disable this.\r\n\r\nStill left to do before this is functional:\r\n- [ ] fix issue that prevents this from working in the editor (weird sampler not recognised as a sampler bug, IDK) \r\n- [ ] optimise compiled variants based on whether deferred rendering is enabled\r\n- [ ] provide access to the cluster data\r\n- [ ] figure out if we can store layer data or our instance index, currently all lights effect all geometry (except unshaded)\r\n- [ ] apply omni and spotlight lighting code\r\n\r\nThe solution does support multiview however there is a pre-existing issue with clustering for which the workaround does not work with deferred rendering. We may need to change the code that builds the clustering to create a cluster buffer per eye.\r\n\r\nThere are many features that apply lighting on a per instance basis or for other reasons can not work with deferred rendering. An incomplete list is below:\r\n- Godot shader user lighting shader code will be ignore, some output of the user fragment shader code will have no effect, we'll need to put together a full list of these\r\n- MSAA can't be used with deferred rendering (at this time, possibly never)\r\n- SSAO/SSR/SSIL etc are likely broken, these may be fixable with a little extra work\r\n- Fog is currently broken, we may be able to introduce this\r\n- `shadow_to_opacity` (unless combined with unshaded) won't work.\r\n- all geometry (except unshaded) receive shadows\r\n- transmittence, rim, clearcoat and similar settings will be ignored\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3918b979-3f40-43f7-8125-e81ec73a84d2)\r\n\r\n- *Bugsquad edit: This partially addresses https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/8295.*","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","u